# 🎯 Software Factory Verification Rules

## 🚨 CRITICAL: VERIFICATION BEFORE CELEBRATION

### ⚠️ MANDATORY VERIFICATION PROTOCOL
Before declaring ANY success or capturing learnings:

1. **FUNCTIONAL VERIFICATION**
   - [ ] Interactive features actually work (forms submit, buttons respond)
   - [ ] Real data processing (not just mock/static displays)
   - [ ] Complete user flows (end-to-end functionality)
   - [ ] Error handling works (graceful failures, not crashes)

2. **TECHNICAL VERIFICATION**
   - [ ] Builds successfully (no compilation errors)
   - [ ] Deploys successfully (production works, not just local)
   - [ ] Performance acceptable (loads in reasonable time)
   - [ ] Cross-platform compatibility verified

3. **BUSINESS LOGIC VERIFICATION**
   - [ ] Calculations accurate (math matches expected results)
   - [ ] Business rules enforced (validation, constraints work)
   - [ ] Data integrity maintained (input/output consistency)
   - [ ] Security verified (no exposed sensitive data)

### 🚫 PROHIBITED ACTIONS
- **NEVER** claim "✅ WORKING" without full verification
- **NEVER** declare "✅ Complete" for partial functionality
- **NEVER** capture learnings from unverified work
- **NEVER** celebrate page loads as functional demos

### 📊 STATUS REPORTING STANDARDS
- **✅ Complete Success**: All verification checks pass, production-ready
- **🟡 Partial Success**: Core functionality works, some features incomplete
- **❌ Not Working**: Basic functionality fails, major bugs present

### 🔄 VERIFICATION PROCESS
1. **Define Success Criteria** before starting work
2. **Test-Driven Development** with verification at each step
3. **Incremental Verification** of each feature as built
4. **Final Validation** before any success declaration

### 🎯 LEARNING CAPTURE GATES
- Only capture learnings from verified successes
- Document what actually works vs. what's just placeholder
- Distinguish between "deployed" and "functional"
- Be honest about limitations and incomplete features

### 🚀 QUALITY METRICS
- Verification coverage percentage
- False positive/negative rates
- Learning accuracy rate
- Time to verification vs. development time

## 🎉 SUCCESS CRITERIA
- No premature celebrations
- All claims verified before stating
- Learnings only from real functionality
- Clear, honest status reporting

**Remember: Verification before celebration. Reality before learnings. Quality before quantity.**

## 🔧 MANDATORY VERIFICATION SCRIPT
Before claiming ANY success, run:
```bash
./project-starter/verify_deployment.sh
```

Only declare success if ALL verifications pass.